# Shared by both images. Dockerfile.fly copies only the backend directories by
# name, so nothing here changes what that image contains — but Dockerfile (the
# self-hosting image) does `COPY . .` to build the frontend, so `src`, `public`
# and `images` must NOT be excluded. images/ holds the wallpapers that
# src/lib/backgrounds.ts imports; excluding it fails the build.
